{
  "id": "autocad",
  "name": "Autodesk AutoCAD",
  "kind": "app",
  "category": "CAD / 3D",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "acad.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "com.autodesk.AutoCAD2025"
    ],
    "window_title": []
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://www.autodesk.com/shortcuts/autocad",
    "https://damassets.autodesk.net/content/dam/autodesk/www/shortcuts/autocad/AutoCAD-Shortcuts-Guide-Autodesk.pdf"
  ],
  "note": "From the Autodesk \"AutoCAD Keyboard Shortcuts Guide\" (autodesk.com/shortcuts/autocad and the PDF it links to), sections \"Toggle General Features\", \"Toggle Drawing Modes\", \"Manage Screen\", \"Manage Workflow\" and \"Manage Drawings\". These are headings rather than modes, so context is \"\". The guide's \"One Key Shortcuts\" and \"Hot Keys A-Z\" lists are command aliases that you type at the command line (A = ARC, Z = ZOOM, ...), not hotkeys, and are deliberately excluded; the F1-F12 toggles and the Ctrl chords above are true hotkeys. The edition of the guide used here has no \"Coordinate Entry\" section. \"Cancel current command\" is documented three ways - Esc, Ctrl+[ and Ctrl+\\ - and only Esc is listed, because two actions cannot share a name in one context. Autodesk's AutoCAD for Mac shortcuts page could not be retrieved (HTTP 403), so no mac chords are claimed; the macOS bundle id is kept in `match` so the profile still recognises the app.",
